Manifest
We distinguish a sidebar extension from ordinary extension by existence of the sidebar_action property in the manifest file.
{
...
"sidebar_action": {
"default_icon": {                      // required
"16": "images/icon16.png"
},
"default_page": "popup.html",          // required
"default_title": "Sidebar Extension",   // optional; shown in tooltip
"use_navigation_bar": true,      // optional; true is default
"mobile_user_agent": true        // [NOT IMPLEMENTED YET] optional; true is default
}
...
}
default_icon is the icon to launch the sidebar extension.
default_page is the local resource path to the initial page of the extension.
default_title is the string shown as the tool tip.
use_navigation_bar is the flag whether the navigation bar is turned on or off, default is true. When you are not using the navigation bar, you must be aware of that your extension page may be navigated to other websites from drag events. To avoid this matter, please refer to How to avoid my extension from changing urls.
mobile_user_agent is weather the extension panel provides mobile or desktop user agent, default is true
if set true the UA will be
Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android 5.0; Nexus 5 Build/WHALE) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/52.0.2743.116 Whale/0.7.31.0 Mobile Safari/537.36 sidebar
otherwise
Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/52.0.2743.116 Whale/0.7.30.0 Safari/537.36 sidebar
versions numbers may vary.
types
